Use for: reading config files, log files, scripts, or any text file.
Supports line limit to avoid reading oversized files.
  Args JSON Schema: {"properties":{"lines":{"description":"Maximum number of lines to read (default: all, max: 500)","type":"integer"},"path":{"description":"The absolute or relative path to the file","type":"string"},"target":{"description":"Target server name. Omit or use 'localhost' for local execution.","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"}
- **file_transfer**: Upload or download a file between this local controller and a remote server via SFTP.
ALWAYS use this tool instead of shell_exec + scp for file transfers.
Reuses the existing authenticated SSH connection — no password prompt, no PTY required.
action=upload: copies local_path on this PC to remote_path on the target server.
action=download: copies remote_path on the target server to local_path on this PC.
Always include 'description' field with a brief Korean explanation.
